./analysis/screening_run_artifacts_after_prompt_update_20260511/full_runs/nemotron3_super_120b_fp8_review_pipeline_all4027_current_watchdog_20260511T1116Z/job_11581/guideline_pilot_raw_completed.csv:17:3457,A comparative survey on large language models for biological data,a comparative survey on large language models for biological data,,,,,"The development of large language models (LLMs)  has grown exponentially since the release of ChatGPT. Large language models have gained attention for their robust performance across various tasks. The ability of LLMs to understand and produce general-purpose language is achieved by training billions of parameters. These models have emerged as a transformative force in increasing natural language understanding, representing an important step toward general artificial intelligence(AI). LLMs have become powerful tools for various tasks, including natural language processing (NLP), machine translation(MT), vision applications, and question-answering(QA). The expanded reach of LLMs goes beyond the conventional linguistic bounds and includes specialized languages created in different scientific disciplines. The intensification of interest in this new subclass of scientifically oriented LLMs has led to the birth of the scientific LLMs. These scientific LLMs are gradually gaining a foothold as an exciting research area for science study. Theoretically, they share a structure in common with general LLMs. In practice, however, they differ regarding input and usage. This paper undertakes an exhaustive effort to study all the scientific LLMs, the types of structures offered, the datasets, the parameters, and the context of use. Our analysis uses a focused lens that focuses on the biological and chemical domains, which enables an in-depth examination of LLMs for textual knowledge, small molecules, macromolecules, proteins, genomic sequences, and combinations. By providing an overview of the technical advances in the field, this survey is a valuable resource for researchers navigating the complex landscape of scientific LLMs.","['R Mousa', 'A Sarabadani', 'T Taami', 'AA Bengari']",2025.0,,,https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202504.2464/download/final_file,['google_scholar'],1,[],1,,crossref_title,184.0,,14,"{""paper_type"": ""review_editorial"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""unclear"", ""text_component_present"": ""unclear"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""unclear"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""review_editorial"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""mixed_signals"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""not_assessed"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_exclude"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract describes a survey/review of LLMs for biological data, not a primary model paper.""}",review_editorial,unclear,unclear,unclear,review_editorial,mixed_signals,none,none,not_assessed,clear_exclude,"The abstract describes a survey/review of LLMs for biological data, not a primary model paper.","{""paper_type"": ""review_editorial"", ""generative_model_present"": ""unclear"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""unclear"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""review_editorial"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""none"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_exclude"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract presents a survey of LLMs for biological data, reviewing existing models without proposing a new generative architecture or providing evidence of a novel foundation model.""}",review_editorial,unclear,unclear,review_editorial,none,not_assessed,not_assessed,none,clear_exclude,"The abstract presents a survey of LLMs for biological data, reviewing existing models without proposing a new generative architecture or providing evidence of a novel foundation model.",EXCLUDE,EXCLUDE,False,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
./analysis/screening_run_artifacts_after_prompt_update_20260511/full_runs/nemotron3_super_120b_fp8_review_pipeline_all4027_current_watchdog_20260511T1116Z/job_11581/guideline_pilot_raw_completed.csv:1570:                  Epigenome-wide association studies (EWAS) has become an indispensable approach for elucidating the epigenetic basis of complex traits. EWAS Open Platform (https://ngdc.cncb.ac.cn/ewas/) includes three main components: EWAS Atlas (curated associations from publications), EWAS Data Hub (normalized DNA methylation array data), and EWAS Toolkit (one-stop analysis services). Here, we present a new release of EWAS Open Platform with the following significant updates and enhancements: (i) Expanded information: EWAS Atlas houses over 800 000 associations and incorporates an additional 17 000 curated causal relationships. EWAS Data Hub contains &amp;gt;180 000 batch-corrected samples, which incorporate data from newly added Illumina MethylationEPIC v2.0 BeadChip (935K) as well as trait-specific methylation profiles. EWAS Toolkit now provides an online batch correction tool and an interactive epigenetic causal network. (ii) Enhanced interoperability: data, knowledge, and toolkit are fully interconnected through a unified retrieval, offering integrated summaries and visualization capabilities. (iii) Artificial intelligence (AI)-based service: the platform is newly equipped with an AI-assisted question-answering service, allowing users to interactively explore EWAS-related questions and generate tailored insights. Taken together, EWAS Open Platform has undergone a significant upgrade across data resources, analytical tools, and service functionalities, offering more advanced support for unraveling complex molecular mechanisms from an epigenomic perspective.","['F Yang', 'Z Xiong', 'W Zong', 'D Kong', 'B Tang']",2026.0,Nucleic Acids …,,https://academic.oup.com/nar/article-abstract/54/D1/D1061/8324953,['google_scholar'],1,[],1,,crossref_title,182.0,2026-03-01_to_2026-04-14,456,"{""paper_type"": ""benchmark_resource"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""unclear"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""unclear"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""benchmark_resource"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""AI-assisted question-answering service"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""AI-assisted question-answering service for EWAS-related questions"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""not_assessed"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_exclude"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The record describes EWAS Open Platform, a resource/database with an AI-assisted question-answering service, not a primary generative text-bio model.""}",benchmark_resource,yes,unclear,unclear,benchmark_resource,none,AI-assisted question-answering service,AI-assisted question-answering service for EWAS-related questions,not_assessed,clear_exclude,"The record describes EWAS Open Platform, a resource/database with an AI-assisted question-answering service, not a primary generative text-bio model.","{""paper_type"": ""application_wrapper"", ""generative_model_present"": ""unclear"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""unclear"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""application_wrapper"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""generative_status_unclear"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""none"", ""boundary_case"": ""wrapper_boundary"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract mentions an AI-assisted question-answering service that generates tailored insights but does not describe a specific generative architecture such as a decoder, autoregressive, or sequence-to-sequence model.""}",application_wrapper,unclear,unclear,application_wrapper,generative_status_unclear,not_assessed,not_assessed,none,wrapper_boundary,"The abstract mentions an AI-assisted question-answering service that generates tailored insights but does not describe a specific generative architecture such as a decoder, autoregressive, or sequence-to-sequence model.",EXCLUDE,EXCLUDE,True,"{""paper_type"": ""unclear"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""yes"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""no"", ""generative_model_present"": ""unclear"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""unclear"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""none"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""paper_type_unclear"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""AI-assisted question-answering service, allowing users to interactively explore EWAS-related questions and generate tailored insights."", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""none"", ""boundary_case"": ""thin_abstract_boundary"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract describes a resource platform with an AI-assisted question-answering service but lacks explicit details on text-bio bridging, generative architecture, and whether it is a benchmark/resource or wrapper, leaving key criteria unresolved.""}",unclear,yes,yes,no,unclear,unclear,none,paper_type_unclear,"AI-assisted question-answering service, allowing users to interactively explore EWAS-related questions and generate tailored insights.",none,none,thin_abstract_boundary,"The abstract describes a resource platform with an AI-assisted question-answering service but lacks explicit details on text-bio bridging, generative architecture, and whether it is a benchmark/resource or wrapper, leaving key criteria unresolved."
