s,yes,none,none,"zero-shot annotation, cross-modal question answering, and interactive, explainable dialogue",aligns pretrained BioFMs as modality encoders and aligns them with LLMs,"enabling richer, generative outputs than existing BioFMs",clear_include,"The abstract describes aligning BioFMs with LLMs via projection layers and instruction tuning, enabling generative outputs such as dialogue and question answering, and leverages pretrained LLMs and BioFMs as foundation models.",PASS,PASS,False,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,PASS|PASS,primary_model_paper,yes,yes,yes,yes,yes,,,,,,,"The abstract describes a new method that aligns biomedical modalities to LLMs via projection layers and instruction tuning, enabling cross-modal QA and dialogue, establishing a substantive text-bio bridge. | The abstract describes aligning BioFMs with LLMs via projection layers and instruction tuning, enabling generative outputs such as dialogue and question answering, and leverages pretrained LLMs and BioFMs as foundation models.",INCLUDE,,,INCLUDE,,,False
./analysis/screening_run_artifacts_after_prompt_update_20260511/full_runs/nemotron3_super_120b_fp8_review_pipeline_all4027_current_watchdog_20260511T1116Z/job_11570/guideline_pilot_results_partial.csv:3571:3199,CellVerse: Do Large Language Models Really Understand Cell Biology?,cellverse do large language models really understand cell biology,,,,2505.07865v1,"Recent studies have demonstrated the feasibility of modeling single-cell data as natural languages and the potential of leveraging powerful large language models (LLMs) for understanding cell biology. However, a comprehensive evaluation of LLMs' performance on language-driven single-cell analysis tasks still remains unexplored. Motivated by this challenge, we introduce CellVerse, a unified language-centric question-answering benchmark that integrates four types of single-cell multi-omics data and encompasses three hierarchical levels of single-cell analysis tasks: cell type annotation (cell-level), drug response prediction (drug-level), and perturbation analysis (gene-level). Going beyond this, we systematically evaluate the performance across 14 open-source and closed-source LLMs ranging from 160M to 671B on CellVerse. Remarkably, the experimental results reveal: (1) Existing specialist models (C2S-Pythia) fail to make reasonable decisions across all sub-tasks within CellVerse, while generalist models such as Qwen, Llama, GPT, and DeepSeek family models exhibit preliminary understanding capabilities within the realm of cell biology. (2) The performance of current LLMs falls short of expectations and has substantial room for improvement. Notably, in the widely studied drug response prediction task, none of the evaluated LLMs demonstrate significant performance improvement over random guessing. CellVerse offers the first large-scale empirical demonstration that significant challenges still remain in applying LLMs to cell biology. By introducing CellVerse, we lay the foundation for advancing cell biology through natural languages and hope this paradigm could facilitate next-generation single-cell analysis.",Fan Zhang; Tianyu Liu; Zhihong Zhu; Hao Wu; Haixin Wang; Donghao Zhou; Yefeng Zheng; Kun Wang; Xian Wu; Pheng-Ann Heng,2025.0,,2025-05-09,,"['arxiv', 'google_scholar']",2,[],2,,,,,1820,"{""paper_type"": ""benchmark_resource"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""no"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""no"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""benchmark_resource"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""not_assessed"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_exclude"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The paper presents CellVerse, a language-centric question-answering benchmark for evaluating existing LLMs on single-cell multi-omics tasks, without introducing a new generative text-bio model.""}",benchmark_resource,yes,no,no,benchmark_resource,none,none,none,not_assessed,clear_exclude,"The paper presents CellVerse, a language-centric question-answering benchmark for evaluating existing LLMs on single-cell multi-omics tasks, without introducing a new generative text-bio model.","{""paper_type"": ""benchmark_resource"", ""generative_model_present"": ""no"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""unclear"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""benchmark_resource"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""none"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_exclude"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The paper introduces a benchmark (CellVerse) for evaluating LLMs on single-cell tasks and does not propose a new generative model; thus it lacks a generative architecture and is a benchmark resource.""}",benchmark_resource,no,unclear,benchmark_resource,none,not_assessed,not_assessed,none,clear_exclude,The paper introduces a benchmark (CellVerse) for evaluating LLMs on single-cell tasks and does not propose a new generative model; thus it lacks a generative architecture and is a benchmark resource.,EXCLUDE,EXCLUDE,False,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,EXCLUDE|EXCLUDE,benchmark_resource,yes,no,no,no,unclear,benchmark_resource,,,,,,"The paper presents CellVerse, a language-centric question-answering benchmark for evaluating existing LLMs on single-cell multi-omics tasks, without introducing a new generative text-bio model. | The paper introduces a benchmark (CellVerse) for evaluating LLMs on single-cell tasks and does not propose a new generative model; thus it lacks a generative architecture and is a benchmark resource.",EXCLUDE,benchmark_resource,,EXCLUDE,benchmark_resource,,False
./analysis/screening_run_artifacts_after_prompt_update_20260511/full_runs/nemotron3_super_120b_fp8_review_pipeline_all4027_current_watchdog_20260511T1116Z/job_11570/guideline_pilot_results_partial.csv:3579:3207,Biology-Instructions: A Dataset and Benchmark for Multi-Omics Sequence Understanding Capability of Large Language Models,biologyinstructions a dataset and benchmark for multiomics sequence understanding capability of large language models,,,,2412.19191v2,"Large language models (LLMs) have shown remarkable capabilities in general domains, but their application to multi-omics biology remains underexplored. To address this gap, we introduce Biology-Instructions, the first large-scale instruction-tuning dataset for multi-omics biological sequences, including DNA, RNA, proteins, and multi-molecules. This dataset bridges LLMs and complex biological sequence-related tasks, enhancing their versatility and reasoning while maintaining conversational fluency. We also highlight significant limitations of current state-of-the-art LLMs on multi-omics tasks without specialized training. To overcome this, we propose ChatMultiOmics, a strong baseline with a novel three-stage training pipeline, demonstrating superior biological understanding through Biology-Instructions. Both resources are publicly available, paving the way for better integration of LLMs in multi-omics analysis. The Biology-Instructions is publicly available at: https://github.com/hhnqqq/Biology-Instructions.",Haonan He; Yuchen Ren; Yining Tang; Ziyang Xu; Junxian Li; Minghao Yang; Di Zhang; Dong Yuan; Tao Chen; Shufei Zhang; Yuqiang Li; Nanqing Dong; Wanli Ouyang; Dongzhan Zhou; Peng Ye,2024.0,,2024-12-26,,"['arxiv', 'google_scholar']",2,[],2,,,,,1828,"{""paper_type"": ""benchmark_resource"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""yes"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""yes"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""benchmark_resource"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""ChatMultiOmics, a strong baseline with a novel three-stage training pipeline"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""dataset bridges LLMs and complex biological sequence-related tasks"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""not_assessed"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_exclude"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The paper introduces a dataset and benchmark for multi-omics sequences and proposes a baseline LLM (ChatMultiOmics), indicating a benchmark/resource focus rather than a primary model paper.""}",benchmark_resource,yes,yes,yes,benchmark_resource,none,"ChatMultiOmics, a strong baseline with a novel three-stage training pipeline",dataset bridges LLMs and complex biological sequence-related tasks,not_assessed,clear_exclude,"The paper introduces a dataset and benchmark for multi-omics sequences and proposes a baseline LLM (ChatMultiOmics), indicating a benchmark/resource focus rather than a primary model paper.","{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""generative_model_present"": ""unclear"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""yes"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""none"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""generative_status_unclear"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""none"", ""boundary_case"": ""generative_boundary"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract mentions LLMs and an instruction-tuning dataset but does not explicitly describe a decoder, autoregressive, or other generative mechanism, leaving generative status unclear. It does provide evidence of foundation-model traits via large-scale pretraining and instruction tuning.""}",primary_model_paper,unclear,yes,none,generative_status_unclear,not_assessed,not_assessed,none,generative_boundary,"The abstract mentions LLMs and an instruction-tuning dataset but does not explicitly describe a decoder, autoregressive, or other generative mechanism, leaving generative status unclear. It does provide evidence of foundation-model traits via large-scale pretraining and instruction tuning.",EXCLUDE,UNCERTAIN,True,"{""paper_type"": ""benchmark_resource"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""yes"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""yes"", ""generative_model_present"": ""unclear"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""yes"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""benchmark_resource"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""generative_status_unclear"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""instruction-tuning dataset"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""bridges LLMs and complex biological sequence-related tasks"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""none"", ""boundary_case"": ""thin_abstract_boundary"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract provides a dataset and benchmark linking LLMs to multi-omics sequences, establishing text and bio components and a bridge, but does not explicitly describe a generative mechanism, leaving generative status uncertain.""}",benchmark_resource,yes,yes,yes,unclear,yes,benchmark_resource,generative_status_unclear,instruction-tuning dataset,bridges LLMs and complex biological sequence-related tasks,none,thin_abstract_boundary,"The abstract provides a dataset and benchmark linking LLMs to multi-omics sequences, establishing text and bio components and a bridge, but does not explicitly describe a generative mechanism, leaving generative status uncertain.",EXCLUDE|UNCERTAIN,benchmark_resource,yes,yes,yes,unclear,yes,benchmark_resource,generative_status_unclear,instruction-tuning dataset,bridges LLMs and complex biological sequence-related tasks,none,thin_abstract_boundary,"The abstract provides a dataset and benchmark linking LLMs to multi-omics sequences, establishing text and bio components and a bridge, but does not explicitly describe a generative mechanism, leaving generative status uncertain.",EXCLUDE,benchmark_resource,,EXCLUDE,benchmark_resource,generative_status_unclear,False
