 ""generative_model_present"": ""yes"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""yes"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""none"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""extensive DNA text corpora"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""Geneformer single cell transcriptomes encoder"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""Conditional DNA Regulatory Sequence Generation"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_include"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract describes conditional DNA regulatory sequence generation using large language models, indicating a generative architecture. It also notes pretraining on extensive DNA text corpora, supporting foundation-model evidence.""}",primary_model_paper,yes,yes,none,none,extensive DNA text corpora,Geneformer single cell transcriptomes encoder,Conditional DNA Regulatory Sequence Generation,clear_include,"The abstract describes conditional DNA regulatory sequence generation using large language models, indicating a generative architecture. It also notes pretraining on extensive DNA text corpora, supporting foundation-model evidence.",PASS,PASS,False,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,PASS|PASS,primary_model_paper,yes,yes,yes,yes,yes,,,,,,,"The paper proposes a multimodal model that integrates Geneformer encoder with GPT-2 via instruction tuning to generate DNA regulatory sequences conditioned on cell context, indicating a primary text-bio generative model. | The abstract describes conditional DNA regulatory sequence generation using large language models, indicating a generative architecture. It also notes pretraining on extensive DNA text corpora, supporting foundation-model evidence.",INCLUDE,,,INCLUDE,,,False
