./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0357.stderr.log:1743:./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0244.stderr.log:1588:./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0096.stderr.log:112:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_000761","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"text_bio_bridge_unclear","decision_rationale":"This is a review of AI applications in natural product science, not a primary model paper. It discusses generative AI and knowledge graphs, but the abstract does not define a specific text-bio model bridge.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review demonstrates the latest developments in AI applications for NP drug discovery and genomics\"; mentions \"generative AI\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000762","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The paper evaluates GPT-3.5/GPT-4 as a curation and question-answering tool over genetics and genomic articles. This is an external LLM wrapper for a bioinformatics task, not a new text-bio foundational model.","evidence_snippet":"\"GPT-based retrieval-augmented generation question-answering system\" for wheat and barley genetics data."},{"record_id":"rec_000763","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract presents a new PEDL+ pipeline that uses deep language models for protein-centered relation extraction and then validates the findings in vivo. The text and biological components are coupled in the method itself.","evidence_snippet":"\"protein-centered relation extraction using deep language models\" together with \"in vivo experimental validation\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000764","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"ChatGPT with GPT-4o is only used to generate and rank hypotheses for cardiotoxicity research. That is an application of an existing LLM, not a substantive text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"\"ChatGPT with GPT-4o was used to generate multiple hypotheses\" and experimental plans."},{"record_id":"rec_000765","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The core contribution is a cancer functional proteomics resource, with an LLM-powered chatbot layered on top. The abstract centers the resource and platform rather than a new candidate model.","evidence_snippet":"\"comprehensive cancer functional proteomics resource\" and \"DrBioRight 2.0, an intuitive bioinformatic platform powered by... large language models\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000766","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a clinically oriented review of computer-aided diagnosis systems for lung cancer. The abstract focuses on imaging and ML/DL systems, not a text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"\"This clinically oriented review synthesizes computer-aided diagnosis across classical imaging, machine learning, and deep learning\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000767","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly says it systematically reviews representative LLMs and their biological applications across genome, transcriptome, and proteome fields. It is a review, not a primary model paper.","evidence_snippet":"\"we first systematically review representative LLMs in the biological domain\" and their \"applications across the genome, transcriptome, and proteome fields\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000768","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a new protein language model-driven framework trained on curated GR sequences and applied at genome scale. The text-sequence model is directly tied to the biological discovery task.","evidence_snippet":"\"deep protein language models\" and a \"deep learning-based GR identification model trained on 74,872 curated GR sequences\"."}]}
