","adjudication_reason":"criterion_unclear_or_reviewer_conflict","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"yes"}}},{"record_id":"rec_000421","title":"The Role of Artificial Intelligence in Modern Biotechnology: A Comprehensive Review","abstract":"AlphaFold 3 was trained using multimodal data, including  Single-cell RNA sequencing  (scRNA-seq) and spatial transcriptomics  Moreover, the Virchow model, a foundation model for","doi":"","year":"2026","venue":"Journal of Applied Biotechnology Reports","sources":["google_scholar"],"first_pass_outputs":{"scope_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_000421","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"unclear","text_component_present":"unclear","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"mixed_signals","decision_rationale":"The title explicitly says comprehensive review. The abstract mentions example models and modalities, but does not present a single primary text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"\"The Role of Artificial Intelligence in Modern Biotechnology: A Comprehensive Review\"; \"AlphaFold 3 ... single-cell RNA sequencing ... Virchow model\""},"architecture_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_000421","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The title explicitly says this is a comprehensive review. The abstract cites existing models and training data rather than describing a new generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"“The Role of Artificial Intelligence in Modern Biotechnology: A Comprehensive Review”"},"python_gate":{"provisional_decision":"ADJUDICATE","provisional_code":"review_editorial","adjudication_reason":"criterion_unclear_or_reviewer_conflict","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"unclear","text_component_present":"unclear","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no"}}},{"record_id":"rec_000422","title":"Geneformer Parallel Adaptation, Training, and Optimization on MLU290","abstract":"The rapid expansion of single-cell transcriptomics necessitates scalable and efficient deep-learning frameworks. These frameworks must process massive datasets and reduce dependency on export-constrained hardware. In this study, we present the porting, optimization, and benchmarking of the Geneformer model on the Cambricon MLU290 intelligent accelerator. This device serves as a high-performance, domestically available alternative to mainstream NVIDIA GPUs. We systematically adapted the PyTorch and transformers codebases to leverage Cambricon’s Torch-MLU and CNCL libraries. This enabled seamless distributed training with enhanced communication and memory management. Experimental results show that the MLU290 delivers a remarkable 1,027,734 training iterations per card in 8-card clusters. This performance outpaces the NVIDIA V100 and RTX 4090 by nearly eightfold in comparable configurations. Communication efficiency consistently exceeded 91% in multimachine settings. Optimization of data loading reduced average iteration time by 7.8%. Detailed profiling revealed that synchronization operations accounted for over 33% of total runtime. This identifies clear targets for further performance improvement. Our findings validate the MLU290 as a cost-effective and scalable accelerator for biomedical AI. This study provides a transferable methodology for hardware-agnostic, large-scale deployment of deep learning models in bioinformatics. The work lays the groundwork for a broader adoption of accessible AI hardware in genomics. Finally, this study also suggests future directions in bottleneck optimization, model generalization, and secure federated learning.","doi":"10.1142/s0129156425407193","year":"2026","venue":"… Journal of High Speed Electronics and …","sources":["google_scholar"],"first_pass_outputs":{"scope_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_000422","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"unclear","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"text_component_unclear","decision_rationale":"This is a hardware port and benchmark of an existing Geneformer model, not a new candidate model. The abstract supports single-cell transcriptomics, but not a clearly described text-language bridge.","evidence_snippet":"\"porting, optimization, and benchmarking of the Geneformer model\"; \"single-cell transcriptomics\""},"architecture_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_000422","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a porting and benchmarking paper for the existing Geneformer model on different hardware. It reports optimization and training throughput, not a new generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"“porting, optimization, and benchmarking of the Geneformer model on the Cambricon MLU290”"},"python_gate":{"provisional_decision":"ADJUDICATE","provisional_code":"application_wrapper","adjudication_reason":"criterion_unclear_or_reviewer_conflict","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"unclear","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no"}}},{"record_id":"rec_000424","title":"Medical Image Understanding Improves Survival Prediction via Visual Instruction Tuning","abstract":"Therefore, in this work, we focus on utilizing multimodal  Merlin: A vision language foundation  model for 3d computed  Pan-cancer integrative histologygenomic analysis via multimodal","doi":"","year":"2026","venu