review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"unclear","text_component_present":"unclear","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no"}}},{"record_id":"rec_000422","title":"Geneformer Parallel Adaptation, Training, and Optimization on MLU290","abstract":"The rapid expansion of single-cell transcriptomics necessitates scalable and efficient deep-learning frameworks. These frameworks must process massive datasets and reduce dependency on export-constrained hardware. In this study, we present the porting, optimization, and benchmarking of the Geneformer model on the Cambricon MLU290 intelligent accelerator. This device serves as a high-performance, domestically available alternative to mainstream NVIDIA GPUs. We systematically adapted the PyTorch and transformers codebases to leverage Cambricon’s Torch-MLU and CNCL libraries. This enabled seamless distributed training with enhanced communication and memory management. Experimental results show that the MLU290 delivers a remarkable 1,027,734 training iterations per card in 8-card clusters. This performance outpaces the NVIDIA V100 and RTX 4090 by nearly eightfold in comparable configurations. Communication efficiency consistently exceeded 91% in multimachine settings. Optimization of data loading reduced average iteration time by 7.8%. Detailed profiling revealed that synchronization operations accounted for over 33% of total runtime. This identifies clear targets for further performance improvement. Our findings validate the MLU290 as a cost-effective and scalable accelerator for biomedical AI. This study provides a transferable methodology for hardware-agnostic, large-scale deployment of deep learning models in bioinformatics. The work lays the groundwork for a broader adoption of accessible AI hardware in genomics. Finally, this study also suggests future directions in bottleneck optimization, model generalization, and secure federated learning.","doi":"10.1142/s0129156425407193","year":"2026","venue":"… Journal of High Speed Electronics and …","sources":["google_scholar"],"first_pass_outputs":{"scope_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_000422","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"unclear","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"text_component_unclear","decision_rationale":"This is a hardware port and benchmark of an existing Geneformer model, not a new candidate model. The abstract supports single-cell transcriptomics, but not a clearly described text-language bridge.","evidence_snippet":"\"porting, optimization, and benchmarking of the Geneformer model\"; \"single-cell transcriptomics\""},"architecture_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_000422","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a porting and benchmarking paper for the existing Geneformer model on different hardware. It reports optimization and training throughput, not a new generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"“porting, optimization, and benchmarking of the Geneformer model on the Cambricon MLU290”"},"python_gate":{"provisional_decision":"ADJUDICATE","provisional_code":"application_wrapper","adjudication_reason":"criterion_unclear_or_reviewer_conflict","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"unclear","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no"}}},{"record_id":"rec_000424","title":"Medical Image Understanding Improves Survival Prediction via Visual Instruction Tuning","abstract":"Therefore, in this work, we focus on utilizing multimodal  Merlin: A vision language foundation  model for 3d computed  Pan-cancer integrative histologygenomic analysis via multimodal","doi":"","year":"2026","venue":"arXiv preprint arXiv …","sources":["google_scholar"],"first_pass_outputs":{"scope_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_000424","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"mixed_signals","decision_rationale":"The abstract points to visual instruction tuning on a medical vision-language foundation model and mentions histology-genomic analysis. It still reads as an application or adaptation of an existing multimodal model rather than a primary text-bio foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"visual instruction tuning\"; \"vision language foundation model\"; \"histologygenomic analysis via multimodal\""},"architecture_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_000424","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract centers on using a vision-language foundation model for image understanding and survival prediction. This is an application of an existing model rather than evidence of a new generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"“utilizing multimodal Merlin: A vision language foundation model” and “survival prediction”"},"python_gate":{"provisional_decision":"ADJUDICATE","provisional_code":"application_wrapper","adjudication_reason":"criterion_unclear_or_reviewer_conflict","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no"}}},{"record_id":"rec_000426","title":"The Cell Ontology in the age of single-cell omics","abstract":"of Large Language Models (LLM) and standardised prompts,  supplemented by longer,  LLM generated, expert reviewed  prioritize multimodal evidence beyond transcriptomics alone,","doi":"","year":"2026","venue":"Scientific data","sources":["google_scholar"],"first_pass_outputs":{"scope_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_000426","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"mixed_signals","decision_rationale":"The title indicates a Cell Ontology resource paper, and the abstract mentions LLMs and prompts in a curation context. It does not clearly present a primary text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"\"The Cell Ontology... LLM generated, expert reviewed... standardized prompts\""},"architecture_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_000426","paper_type":"unclear","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"paper_type_unclear","decision_rationale":"The abstract fragment only mentions LLM-generated, expert-reviewed content and does not clearly describe a model paper. There is no clear evidence of a novel generative architecture or foundation-model characteristics.","evidence_snippet":"“LLM generated, expert reviewed” and “standardised prompts”"},"python_gate":{"provisional_decision":"ADJUDICATE","provisional_code":"benchmark_resource","adjudication_reason":"criterion_unclear_or_reviewer_conflict","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear"}}}]
