ce","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a benchmark for evaluating LLMs on single-cell tasks, not a primary model paper. It packages multi-omics QA tasks and reports model performance across LLMs.","evidence_snippet":"\"we introduce CellVerse, a unified language-centric question-answering benchmark\" and \"systematically evaluate\" 14 LLMs"},{"record_id":"rec_003029","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is an LLM workflow for single-cell annotation using a graph-structured marker database, not a new foundational model. The LLM is wrapped around retrieval and annotation steps.","evidence_snippet":"\"domain-specific knowledge graph retrieval-augmented LLMs workflow for single-cell annotation\""},{"record_id":"rec_003030","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This proposes a new probabilistic CCA method for multi-modal data integration. The abstract is about bioinformatics and cancer data, but it does not describe any text/language component.","evidence_snippet":"\"multi-modal data integration\" and application to \"TCGA cancer datasets\" with \"no text component\" described"},{"record_id":"rec_003031","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a conversational bioinformatics platform that uses LLMs to generate and execute analysis code. It is an application framework rather than a new text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"\"platform that enables researchers to perform bioinformatics analyses using natural language\" and \"generates and executes bioinformatics code\""},{"record_id":"rec_003032","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is explicitly a survey of LLMs in bioinformatics, so it is not a primary model paper. It summarizes prior work across DNA, RNA, proteins, and single-cell data.","evidence_snippet":"\"Large Language Models in Bioinformatics: A Survey\" and \"This survey provides a systematic review of recent advancements\""}]}
